From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:55:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/pc80/rtc: A POST code for a reset the firmware asks
 for

With CMOS_POST, the next boot reports the last POST code of a boot that
did not reach the payload or the OS as that of a hung boot, and the
event log records it (ELOG_TYPE_LAST_POST_CODE). A reset that a setting
needs, before the payload, ends a boot as well, and is then logged as a
hang at every boot that does it.

Add POSTCODE_RESET_REQUESTED (0xfc) for the code right before such a
reset, which cmos_post_previous_boot() takes as a normal end of a boot,
and which the code after the reset can read back with the extra field
to tell its own reset from another one.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init.

Change-Id: I3ffb5217583807bf35ce964f26cf252516b9e6ab
---
 src/commonlib/include/commonlib/console/post_codes.h | 9 +++++++++
 src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c                          | 1 +
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/commonlib/include/commonlib/console/post_codes.h b/src/commonlib/include/commonlib/console/post_codes.h
index b0f9565e35..4b3e0a6a05 100644
--- a/src/commonlib/include/commonlib/console/post_codes.h
+++ b/src/commonlib/include/commonlib/console/post_codes.h
@@ -459,6 +459,15 @@
  */
 #define POSTCODE_ENTER_ELF_BOOT				0xf8
 
+/**
+ * \brief Final code before a reset the firmware asks for
+ *
+ * Called right before a reset that a setting needs, not one after an error: the
+ * next boot does not report it as the last code of a hung boot. CMOS_POST keeps
+ * who asked for it in the extra field.
+ */
+#define POSTCODE_RESET_REQUESTED			0xfc
+
 /**
  * \brief Final code before OS resumes
  *
diff --git a/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c b/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c
index ca53005344..4ad38b87ae 100644
--- a/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c
+++ b/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@ int cmos_post_previous_boot(u8 *code, u32 *extra)
 	case POSTCODE_OS_BOOT:
 	case POSTCODE_OS_RESUME:
 	case POSTCODE_ENTER_ELF_BOOT:
+	case POSTCODE_RESET_REQUESTED:
 	case 0:
 		break;
 	default:
-- 
